<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James III of Majorca</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1315">1315</a>–<a href="/years/1349">1349</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James III was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mallorca">Majorca</a> from 1324 to 1344, ruling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a> and the lordship of Montpellier. His cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-iv-of-aragon">Peter IV of Aragon</a> seized his kingdom in 1343–1344 and absorbed it into the Crown of Aragon. To finance a reconquest, James sold Montpellier to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-vi-of-france">Philip VI of France</a> in 1349, and he was killed the same year at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-llucmajor">Battle of Llucmajor</a> trying to retake Majorca.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-iii-of-majorca.jpg" alt="James III of Majorca" width="201" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_III_of_Majorca_on_his_throne.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
